    sharedBottleneck: pair("UP-605는 signed wafer record가 최신의 유일한 process history인지 알아야 lineage error와 model error를 나눈다. UP-315는 finite signed record의 observation map이 injective인지 알아야 history를 하나로 복원한다. 두 문제 모두 local authenticity만으로는 rollback·fork·erased cause·pre-witness falsehood를 구별하지 못하며, retained state와 observer 간 view 비교가 추가돼야 한다.", "UP-605 must know whether a signed wafer record names the current unique process history before separating lineage error from model error. UP-315 must know whether the observation map of a finite signed record is injective before reconstructing one history. In both problems, local authenticity alone cannot distinguish rollback, forks, erased causes, or pre-witness falsehood; retained state and observer-to-observer view comparison are additional necessary coordinates."),
    mapping: pair("Wafer/chamber trigger ↔ physical event index, capture·export·package commitment ↔ observation boundary, equipment restart ↔ counter-domain transition, fab/vendor receipt view ↔ retained candidate history, independent receiver digest ↔ earliest physical witness로 대응한다. Accepted tree head와 spent nonce는 각각 freshness와 transition monotonicity의 state variable이다.", "The mapping is wafer or chamber trigger to physical event index, capture/export/package commitment to observation boundary, equipment restart to counter-domain transition, fab or vendor receipt view to retained candidate history, and independent receiver digest to earliest physical witness. The accepted tree head and spent nonce are state variables for freshness and transition monotonicity, respectively."),
    transfer: pair("두 분야에 같은 verdict lattice를 적용한다. Evidence preimage가 하나면 exact, 여러 개면 candidate set, currentness·global view가 부족하면 refuse, 이미 소비된 transition이면 reject, 최초 독립 witness 앞이면 outside로 기록한다. Proof bytes와 application causal claim을 분리해 valid receipt가 곧 verified physical history라는 과잉주장을 막는다.", "Apply the same verdict lattice in both fields. Return exact when the evidence preimage is one, a candidate set when several histories survive, refuse when currentness or global-view evidence is absent, reject a consumed transition, and mark truth before the first independent witness outside coverage. Separating proof bytes from the application causal claim prevents a valid receipt from being overclaimed as a verified physical history."),
    minimumTest: pair("Crash-safe head/nonce store와 별도 운영자 두 명의 transparency view를 만들고 replay·backup rollback·same-nonce fork·split view를 blind 주입한다. 그 뒤 정상 capture보다 앞선 독립 witness가 있는 acquisition 한 건에서 event와 payload join을 검증하고 common-cause audit를 수행한다.", "Build a crash-safe head and nonce store plus transparency views operated by two separate parties, then blind-inject replay, backup rollback, same-nonce forks, and split views. Afterward, verify the event and payload join in one acquisition with an independent witness ahead of ordinary capture and perform a common-cause audit."),
    failureBoundary: pair("Record가 여러 event를 적분하거나 후보 transformation grammar가 불완전하면 one-to-one injectivity 결과가 깨진다. 모든 observer가 같은 fork를 받거나 witness와 writer가 전원·firmware·관리자를 공유하면 비교와 signature 수를 늘려도 물리 truth는 나타나지 않는다. 이 연결은 lineage confounder를 좁힐 뿐 semiconductor physics나 역사 X16 identity 자체를 해결하지 않는다.", "The one-to-one injectivity result breaks when a record integrates several events or the candidate transformation grammar is incomplete. If every observer receives the same fork, or witness and writer share power, firmware, and administration, more comparisons and signatures still do not reveal physical truth. This connection contracts a lineage confounder; it does not solve semiconductor physics or recover historical X16 identity."),
    evidence: pair("Node와 Python은 44개 causal verdict와 aggregate에 exact 합의했다. Cross-view arm은 27개 composite를 exact하게 좁히고 3개 shadow를 set으로, 7개 rollback/fork를 refusal로, 2개 bridge conflict를 rejection으로, 2개 collusion을 outside로 남겼다. 세 번째 parser는 27개 positive와 54개 negative control, 두 independent receipt attachment를 검증했다.", "Node and Python agree exactly on forty-four causal verdicts and their aggregates. The cross-view arm contracts twenty-seven composites exactly, leaves three shadows as sets, seven rollback or fork cases as refusals, two bridge conflicts as rejections, and two collusion cases outside coverage. A third parser validates twenty-seven positive and fifty-four negative controls plus attachment of two independent receipts."),
